  "description": "LUFDEY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H184 Ce6 O40. From the CIF bond table, CE1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; CE2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; CE3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.759-3.859 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.89-113.23°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Ce6O4(OH)4(OCOCH2tBu)12(HOCOCH2tBu)4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
